        <mxCell id="o-e14" value="notify" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;endArrow=block;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="o-notif" target="o-pager">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="o-trade" value="&lt;b&gt;Key Trade-offs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Label index + S3 chunks (Loki-style) vs full-text Elasticsearch:&lt;/b&gt; ES gives fast arbitrary search, but its index is ~raw size and indexing CPU dominates at 1.5 PB/month; label-only indexing is an order of magnitude cheaper and survives 10×, at the cost of slower unscoped content search → make service + time mandatory. (ClickHouse with bloom-filter skip indexes is the middle ground.)&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Kafka hash partitioning vs per-host:&lt;/b&gt; per-host ordering buys nothing (queries sort by ts) and makes a noisy host a hot partition.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Stream-evaluated alerts vs polling the store:&lt;/b&gt; polling = 83 scans/s competing with humans and minutes of latency; streaming = seconds, zero search load, at the cost of only supporting windowed aggregations over the live stream.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Ack after Kafka (at-least-once) vs ack after index:&lt;/b&gt; lower ingest latency + HA; duplicates removed by (batchId, offset) dedupe in the indexer." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="2900" width="1730" height="160" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="o-dd" value="&lt;b&gt;Deep Dives&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. &lt;b&gt;Core problem: content search over 1.5 PB under 5 s p99.&lt;/b&gt; Naive: time-partitioned store scans everything in range (7 days ≈ 350 TB) → fails. Fix: prune by service + time + per-chunk bloom filter so a scoped query touches GBs, then parallel-scan those chunks across the querier fleet, early-terminating at limit. Return partial=true rather than blow the SLA.&lt;br&gt;2. &lt;b&gt;10× (15 PB hot):&lt;/b&gt; indexing throughput + cost break first for full-text; label-only indexing scales linearly with S3; add per-service ingest quotas, sampling of DEBUG level, and tiered retention by level.&lt;br&gt;3. &lt;b&gt;Hot keys:&lt;/b&gt; a noisy service floods its chunks → per-service quotas at the gateway, split chunks by labels + time, hash-partition Kafka.&lt;br&gt;4. &lt;b&gt;Consistency:&lt;/b&gt; at-least-once end to end, deduped at the indexer; logs searchable within ~seconds (freshness SLO), not instantly.&lt;br&gt;5. &lt;b&gt;Operability:&lt;/b&gt; freshness canary, lag alerts, loss reconciliation (agent dropped vs ingested vs indexed), DLQ for malformed batches, per-tier cost dashboard; the alert pipeline gets its own dead-man's-switch alert." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fillColor=#fafafa;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="3090" width="1730" height="180" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
